// Recorded by KataGo itself: the VERSION 7 block of the "NN Inputs V3V4V5V6 Basic"
// section of cpp/tests/results/runOutputTests.txt, which its own test binary
// generates from cpp/tests/testnninputs.cpp.
//
// The position is the end of the 159 move 19x19 game below, white to move, komi 7.5,
// under Tromp-Taylor rules (positional superko, area scoring, multi-stone suicide
// legal). One string per spatial channel, one character per point in row-major
// order. Channels 6, 7, 8, 20 and 21 are all zeros here: no ko ban stands at the end
// of this game and nothing in it reaches the encore, which is what lets a port that
// models neither superko nor the encore be checked against it.
